  "summary": "Napoleon's new army, crossing the Saale towards Leipzig, sent Ney's corps over the Rippach, a stream in a ravine lined with villages, to cover its right. Lanskoi's Russian cavalry fell back from the far bank, but Winzingerode's guns fired across the ravine on Souham's conscripts, packed in dense columns. At noon Napoleon came up and sent the Guard cavalry forward to drive off the guns; Marshal Bessières, riding ahead to look at the ground, was killed by a roundshot. The Russians gave way, and by evening Ney's corps was round Lützen, where the allies attacked it the next day.",
